/**
 * Enters up to 100 readings. Each row is saved in its own transaction, so one refused row never undoes another;
 * the answer is 200 with one result per row in request order (`SAVED` or `REJECTED` with `error`). A reading
 * counts at once (status `APPROVED`, source `ENTERED`). `takenOn` absent means today in Europe/Kyiv. A counted
 * reading of the same meter and date is replaced: it stays in the history as `SUPERSEDED` and its id is in
 * `supersededReadingIds`; the same value on the same date again changes nothing. Row error codes: `NOT_FOUND`
 * (`meterId`: no such meter in the cooperative), `READING_DATE_IN_FUTURE` (`takenOn`, params `today`),
 * `READING_DATE_OUTSIDE_METER` (`takenOn`, params `installedOn` and, for a removed meter, `removedOn`),
 * `READING_OUT_OF_ORDER` (`value`: lower than the previous counted point or higher than the next one; params
 * `previousTakenOn` and `previousValue`, or `nextTakenOn` and `nextValue`), `READING_IN_USE` (a charge uses the
 * readings around the date). A saved row may carry the warning `UNUSUAL_CONSUMPTION`: the daily consumption of
 * the interval it closes is more than 3 times the daily average over the meter's counted intervals that ended in
 * the 180 days before it (none without such an interval). 400 `VALIDATION_FAILED` for the whole request when a
 * row is malformed (`rows[i].value` `METER_VALUE_INVALID`, `rows` `REQUIRED` or `TOO_LONG`). Requires
 * `READINGS_ENTER`; each saved row is written to the audit log (`READING_ENTERED`, or `READING_REPLACED` when it
 * replaced a reading of the same date, with `photo` `false`). No row needs a photo, whatever the setting
 * `readingPhotoRequired`; one reading with a photo is entered through `enterReadingWithPhoto`.
 * @summary Enter readings, one or a whole round
 */
